{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793199908,"nonce":"+KXZ2d7aX+QSnRxaw0BJHlDTnTk=","title":"A long or deeply nested CEL expression in a Pipeline aborts scarab-server","message":"Found by the ADR-0075 CEL spike (branch spike/cel-type-checker), 2026-10-28.\n\nThe CEL parser recurses; a stack overflow aborts the whole process and catch_unwind cannot catch it. A repository author controls the expression text (when:, ${{ }}), so a Pipeline can take down the control plane at compile time.\n\n- cel-interpreter 0.10 (main today): about 1,000 nested parentheses abort a release build.\n- cel 0.15: nesting is capped at depth 96 (parse error), but a left-recursive chain of about 5,000 links (a.b.b..., x + x...), about 10 KB, still aborts in release. In debug builds the 0.15 parser overflows a 2 MiB thread at about 12 nested calls.\n\nFix (ADR-0075 §6): cap CEL source length for Pipeline expressions (4 KiB, as for policy rules), and run all CEL parsing on a thread with a large stack. Add a regression test with a 10 KB left-recursive chain.","files":null}]}